==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionGate  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionGate.als
    rationale: Removing the permission gate lets a Success outcome occur on a (role, op) cell that is not in the matrix. Injecting a CustomerRole caller succeeding at OpGetAudit (denied by the matrix) is a direct counterexample to least-privilege, customer-action-scope, and the no-audit-for-customers rule.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerActionScope, FR_021_OfficerIdHiddenFromCustomer
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerActionScope: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_021_OfficerIdHiddenFromCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryExists  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntryExists.als
    rationale: Removing the existence half of audit-trail completeness lets the model invent an application that has reached UnderReview with zero audit entries — violating completeness, the submission-audit guarantee, and retention.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_009_SubmissionAudit, FR_019_OneAuditPerTransition, FR_022_AuditRetained
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_SubmissionAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_OneAuditPerTransition: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_022_AuditRetained: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditNoDuplicates  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditNoDuplicates.als
    rationale: Removing duplicate-prevention lets the model fabricate two distinct audit entries recording the same applied transition for one application — the canonical append-only / no-rewrites violation.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoLeakNotFound  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_NoLeakNotFound.als
    rationale: Removing the no-leak/no-foreign-read constraint lets a customer successfully GET an application owned by another customer, violating both ownership-based access and the no-existence-leak rule.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_020_CustomerSeesOwnOnly
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_CustomerSeesOwnOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecideOnlyByAssigned  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecideOnlyByAssigned.als
    rationale: Removing the assigned-officer gate on Decide lets a non-assigned loan officer successfully decide somebody else's claimed application — precisely SC-005's never-event.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedDecides
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing the in-flight uniqueness fact lets the same customer have two simultaneous Submitted/UnderReview applications, breaking FR-008's partial unique index invariant.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

